erates through U.S. and International Franchise segments. Its restaurant portfolio has four concepts, including Outback Steakhouse, a casual steakhouse restaurant; Carrabba's Italian Grill that offers authentic Italian cuisine; Bonefish Grill; and Fleming's Prime Steakhouse & Wine Bar, a contemporary steakhouse. Bloomin' Brands, Inc. was founded in 1988 and is based in Tampa, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael  Spanos | CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 64K people. Revenue per employee of $62K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $2K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $122 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 35\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Bloomin' Brands, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $889M market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $97M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 33.59\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 25% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 63% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 22% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Shareholders Will Be Pleased With The Qual